    <section class="step" style="--step-bg:#EAF0FF">
      <div class="wrap step-inner">
        <div class="copy">
          <p class="eyebrow">Depth 1 · Under the sleeve</p>
          <h2>She's wearing two medical devices</h2>
          <p>A sensor on her arm reads her sugar level every few minutes. A pump at her waist delivers insulin through a thin tube. She wears them day and night and replaces them herself.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="step" style="--step-bg:#C4D3FF">
      <div class="wrap step-inner">
        <div class="copy">
          <p class="eyebrow">Depth 2 · In the bag</p>
          <h2>She never leaves home without a kit</h2>
          <p>A backup insulin pen in case the pump fails. A meter to double-check the sensor. Juice and glucose tablets for lows. Spares of everything. Forgetting it can mean turning around and going home.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="step dark" style="--step-bg:#2847B8">
      <div class="wrap step-inner">
        <div class="copy">
          <p class="eyebrow">Depth 3 · On the phone</p>
          <h2>Her phone is a medical monitor</h2>
          <p>The sensor sends a reading to her phone all day, and alarms don't wait for a good moment. This one arrived on Tuesday, five minutes before a meeting she was leading.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="step dark" style="--step-bg:#1B2F78">
      <div class="wrap step-inner">
        <div class="copy">
          <p class="eyebrow">Depth 4 · In her head</p>
          <h2>Every meal starts with maths</h2>
          <p>Before the first bite tonight, Priya works through all of this, and nobody at the table notices. A Stanford Medicine article put it at about 180 health-related decisions a day.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="step dark" style="--step-bg:#0E1633">
