          <h2>It doesn't stop at night</h2>
          <p>3:07 am. An alarm says she's low. She walks to the kitchen, drinks juice, and waits fifteen minutes to check again. By 3:30 she's back in bed. At 9 she's at her desk, and nobody knows.</p>
        </div>
